<!-- wp:paragraph {"fontSize":"large"} --><p class="has-large-font-size">Robert E. Burns American Legion Post 165 is a local veterans organization serving Two Rivers, Wisconsin.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">What the Legion Does</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The American Legion continues service after military life by supporting veterans, families, youth, responsible citizenship, remembrance, and community service.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">The Four Pillars</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>These four pillars guide the Legion's work: helping veterans get care and support, backing a strong and safe country, teaching respect for our flag and country, and looking out for kids and young people.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:list --><ul><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Veterans Affairs and Rehabilitation:</strong> help veterans get the benefits and care they earned.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>National Security:</strong> support a strong defense and community readiness.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Americanism:</strong> show respect for the flag, the Constitution, and civic duty.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Children and Youth:</strong> invest in safe, healthy opportunities for the next generation.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->
<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Serving Two Rivers</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We show up for local events, help veterans stay connected, and look for practical ways to be useful in the community.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Where We Meet</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Post 165 meets at Manitowoc Rifle &amp; Pistol Club. It is our meeting location, not the center of the post's identity.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
